   "evidence": "`mathlib/Mathlib/Logic/Function/Basic.lean:456`: `theorem RightInverse.leftInverse {f g} (h : RightInverse g f) : LeftInverse f g := h` \u2014 proof is `h`, i.e. the two are the same proposition. Compare Functoriality.lean:93-98 with 102-107.",
   "file": "TauCeti/LinearAlgebra/SymmetricAlgebra/Functoriality.lean",
   "fix": "Delete `map_rightInverse`; callers wanting the right-inverse form use `map_leftInverse R h` directly (it elaborates against `Function.RightInverse` since the two are definitionally equal).",
   "issue": "`map_rightInverse` is the same statement as `map_leftInverse` (line 93) with `f` and `g` swapped: `Function.RightInverse (map R g) (map R f)` *is* `Function.LeftInverse (map R f) (map R g)` by definition, and the hypothesis `f.comp g = LinearMap.id` is `map_leftInverse`'s hypothesis at the swapped instantiation. The proof body is a character-for-character copy with `f`/`g` exchanged.",
   "line": 102
  },
  {
   "evidence": "`mathlib/Mathlib/LinearAlgebra/SymmetricAlgebra/Basic.lean:119-123` `@[ext 1200] theorem algHom_ext`; `Basic.lean:99` `def lift : (M \u2192\u2097[R] A) \u2243 (SymmetricAlgebra R M \u2192\u2090[R] A)`; Functoriality.lean:72-73 shows the reverse direction is `map_\u03b9` verbatim. grep for `map_unique` in `code/TauCeti` returns only this declaration (other hits are unrelated `TriangulatedK0`/`AbelianK0` lemmas).",
   "file": "TauCeti/LinearAlgebra/SymmetricAlgebra/Functoriality.lean",
   "fix": "Delete `map_unique`; uniqueness is already `SymmetricAlgebra.algHom_ext` (plus the `@[simp]` `map_\u03b9`), and `SymmetricAlgebra.lift` is an `Equiv`, so `g = map R f` is decided by `lift.injective`. If a uniqueness lemma is wanted, keep only the `\u2192` direction (`(h : \u2200 a, g (\u03b9 R M a) = \u03b9 R N (f a)) : g = map R f`).",
   "issue": "`map_unique` bundles two already-available facts: the `\u2190` direction is literally `map_\u03b9` (its proof is `rintro rfl; exact map_\u03b9 R f`), and the `\u2192` direction is a one-line application of Mathlib's `@[ext]` lemma `SymmetricAlgebra.algHom_ext` together with `map_\u03b9`. It has no consumer in the repo.",
   "line": 62
  }
 ],
